Ryujinx shader translator: AstOptimizer propagated the temporaries StructuredProgram makes for SPIR-V call arguments
back into the Call, so GenerateCall got an expression or an undeclared operand instead of a local (InvalidCastException /
KeyNotFoundException in GetLocalPointer: the TexelFetchScale calls of texel fetches). Uses inside a Call are no longer
replaced; the temporary and its assignment stay. Was worked around by the harness's DebugMode retry ("ok-retry"), which
also turns off the global-to-storage-buffer pass. The Ryujinx code in the context lines is MIT.
Second change: an assignment whose result is never read was deleted together with its operation, so atomics with
an unused result (RED, ATOMS.POPC.INC to RZ) vanished from optimised output (only DebugMode kept them); assignments
from atomics and calls now stay.
Third change: a value read from memory (storage, shared, local, global, image) or returned by an atomic or a call was
propagated into its single use even when a store, atomic, call or barrier came in between, which moved the read past the
write ("x = buf[i]; buf[i] = y; use(x)" read the new value). Such a value is now propagated only into the next statements
of the same block when nothing in between can write memory; otherwise it stays in its local. An atomic or call result
is never propagated: the second change keeps its assignment, so propagating it ran the atomic twice (hwcheck: ATOMG.ADD
returned the value after its own add and added twice).
